@startuml EUDI_Reuse_Checklist
!define COMPLETE #90EE90
!define OPTIONAL #FFD700

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor white
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #2C5F77

title EUDI Wallet - Reusable Architecture Checklist

rectangle "**PRESENTATION LAYER**" as presentation {
  rectangle "React Native setup" as rn COMPLETE
  rectangle "TypeScript 5.3+ config" as ts COMPLETE
  rectangle "UI component library" as ui OPTIONAL

  note right of presentation
    **Reuse**
    - Project structure and tsconfig
    - Navigation patterns
    - State management approach

    **Customize**
    - Branding and themes
    - Localization (i18n)
    - Accessibility features
  end note
}

rectangle "**BUSINESS LOGIC LAYER**" as business {
  rectangle "KeyManager module" as km COMPLETE
  rectangle "OpenID4VCI client" as vci COMPLETE
  rectangle "OpenID4VP client" as vp COMPLETE
  rectangle "SD-JWT handler" as sdjwt COMPLETE
  rectangle "Protocol validators" as validators COMPLETE

  note right of business
    **Reuse**
    - All protocol implementations
    - Repository pattern structure
    - Strategy pattern for key storage
    - Factory pattern for JWT creation

    **Customize**
    - Issuer-specific metadata
    - Supported credential types
    - Presentation definitions
  end note
}

rectangle "**DATA LAYER**" as data {
  rectangle "CredentialStore schema" as schema COMPLETE
  rectangle "SQLite indexes" as indexes COMPLETE
  rectangle "Query patterns" as queries COMPLETE
  rectangle "SQLCipher integration" as cipher OPTIONAL

  note right of data
    **Reuse**
    - Database schema and indexes
    - Parameterized query patterns
    - Expiry cleanup logic

    **Customize**
    - Additional metadata fields
    - Backup/restore strategies
    - Encryption layer
  end note
}

rectangle "**NATIVE LAYER**" as native {
  rectangle "Keychain wrapper (iOS)" as keychain COMPLETE
  rectangle "Keystore wrapper (Android)" as keystore COMPLETE
  rectangle "NFC DNIe reader" as nfc COMPLETE
  rectangle "MRZ scanner" as mrz COMPLETE

  note right of native
    **Reuse**
    - Hardware key storage abstractions
    - ICAO 9303 BAC implementation
    - MRZ validation logic

    **Customize**
    - Support for other ID cards
    - Additional NFC data groups
    - Camera optimization
  end note
}

rectangle "**SECURITY CONTROLS**" as security {
  rectangle "Input validation" as input COMPLETE
  rectangle "Signature verification" as sig COMPLETE
  rectangle "Zero trust principles" as zt COMPLETE
  rectangle "Tampering detection" as tamper OPTIONAL

  note right of security
    **Reuse**
    - All validation layers
    - Signature verification flow
    - Defense in depth approach

    **Customize**
    - Certificate pinning list
    - Attestation requirements
    - Biometric policies
  end note
}

rectangle "**TESTING STRATEGY**" as testing {
  rectangle "Unit test patterns" as unit OPTIONAL
  rectangle "Integration test fixtures" as fixtures OPTIONAL
  rectangle "E2E test scenarios" as e2e OPTIONAL

  note right of testing
    **Reuse**
    - Test structure and mocks
    - Fixture data generators
    - Contract test approach

    **Customize**
    - Issuer-specific test data
    - Network stubs
    - Performance benchmarks
  end note
}

presentation -down-> business
business -down-> data
data -down-> native
security -right-> business
testing -down-> business

legend right
  |= **Priority** |= **Description** |
  | <back:COMPLETE>Complete</back> | Ready to reuse as-is |
  | <back:OPTIONAL>Optional</back> | Enhance or replace |
endlegend

note bottom
  **Implementation Checklist**

  **Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1-2)**
  ☑ Fork or clone base architecture
  ☑ Configure React Native environment
  ☑ Set up TypeScript with strict mode
  ☑ Initialize SQLite database with schema

  **Phase 2: Core Integration (Week 3-4)**
  ☑ Integrate KeyManager with platform keystores
  ☑ Configure OpenID4VCI issuer endpoints
  ☑ Test credential issuance flow end-to-end
  ☑ Implement CredentialStore queries

  **Phase 3: Security Hardening (Week 5-6)**
  ☑ Enable SQLCipher table encryption
  ☑ Implement certificate pinning
  ☑ Add key attestation validation
  ☑ Deploy tampering detection

  **Phase 4: Testing & Validation (Week 7-8)**
  ☑ Run OpenID conformance tests
  ☑ Perform security audit
  ☑ Load testing with production volumes
  ☑ Accessibility compliance check

  **Total effort: 8-10 weeks for production-ready wallet**
end note

@enduml
